   In scope

  The use of an intigriti.me address is mandatory at all times!

   We are happy to announce our program! We've done our best to clean most of
   our known issues and now would like to request your help to spot the once
   we missed! We are specifically looking for

     * CVE-2021- 44228 and all Log4Shell relating issues
     * leaking of personal data
     * horizontal / vertical privilege escalation
     * SQLi

   IMPORTANT:
   Some websites partially share the same codebase and can contain common
   issues. If a specific issue has already been found in another Port of
   Antwerp-Bruges website it will be treated as a duplicate.

   Third‑party software, configuration, and integration
   We value all reports that help us improve our security, including those
   involving third‑party products that we use in our environment. To keep
   expectations clear and fair, we distinguish between vendor issues and
   issues caused by how we deploy or use these products.

    1. Third‑party product vulnerabilities
       If a vulnerability is inherent to a third‑party product (SaaS or
       on‑prem) and is already known, documented, or acknowledged by the
       vendor (for example via a CVE, security advisory, or release notes),
       it will normally not be eligible for a reward under this program.
       In practice, if the issue can be reproduced generically in the
       product, outside of our environment, we will treat it as a vendor
       issue. We still appreciate receiving a report in such cases and may
       forward or coordinate it with the vendor, but we do not guarantee a
       bounty.

    2. Our configuration, integration, and usage
       Vulnerabilities that arise from our own configuration, deployment,
       integration, or usage of third‑party products are in scope and can be
       eligible for rewards.
       Typical examples include misconfigured access controls, insecure
       exposure of admin or management interfaces, weak or hard‑coded
       settings in our deployment, or integration flaws that lead to
       privilege escalation, data access, or other security impact
       specifically in our environment.

    3. How to position your report
       To help us assess your finding fairly and quickly, please clarify
       whether the issue depends on our configuration, integration, or usage,
       or whether it is a generic product vulnerability.
       Where possible, include:

     * Steps to reproduce the issue specifically in our environment

     * Any indicators that the problem is tied to our setup (for example,
       only occurs with our domain, tenant, or specific integration)

     * If you believe a known vendor issue has unique or higher impact
       because of how we use the product, please explain that impact clearly
       — we may still treat such cases more flexibly.

   We aim to be transparent and respectful towards researchers. Even when a
   finding falls outside our reward scope, we will do our best to acknowledge
   your contribution and, where appropriate, coordinate with the relevant
   vendor. In exceptional cases, where we consider the effort and impact of
   your research to be particularly valuable, we may, at our discretion,
   grant a goodwill bonus, even if the finding is formally out of scope.

  Rewards

   Port of Antwerp-Bruges SWAG will be awarded for valid High+ submissions

   Feedback
   Would you like to help us improve our program or have some feedback to
